<urn:atm:triage:finding/AD15-DAEMONRUNTIME-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AD15-DAEMONRUNTIME-001" ;
  triage:title "advisory_runtime.rs daemon-side session runtime never deleted" ;
  triage:description "crates/atm-daemon/src/advisory_runtime.rs is still a fully wired, live 941-line session-lifecycle runtime (register/unregister/fetch/drain/stream, TTL sweep worker, 8 passing tests), implementing GraftPostSendPort and consumed from the live post-send path. AD.14's own fix batch (826b9804) added MAX_ADVISORY_SESSIONS capacity logic ON TOP of this runtime rather than deleting it, entrenching the forbidden concept further. Originally reported during AD14-QA-3 review of PR #478 as ARCH-003, but sprint-AD14.md's scope explicitly excludes crates/atm-daemon/* and defers daemon runtime deletion. sprint-AD15.md's own stated Goal is 'delete daemon-owned graft advisory runtime,' with Exact Targets covering crates/atm-daemon/* and Paths-To-Delete explicitly naming advisory_runtime.rs and its routing in runtime_health.rs/local_ipc_transport*.rs. AD15-FIX-1 (cf3b1e71, verified in AD15-QA-2) only touched atm-graft's CLIENT side crates/atm-graft/src/{lib,transport,runtime}.rs -- the daemon-side deletion that was AD.15's own explicit target was apparently never done, and AD15-QA-2's review-targets never covered it. Team-lead has ruled (user-confirmed 2026-07-06) that this finding is properly AD.15-owned undone work, not an AD.14 violation -- reclassify accordingly rather than treating it as newly discovered on AD.14's branch, and reopen AD.15 for this specific gap." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AD" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "ARCH" ;
  triage:severity "Blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "fixed_partial" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-06T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AD15-DAEMONRUNTIME-001/s14/1> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s14/826b980> ;
  triage:fixedOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s15/cf3b1e7> ;
  triage:promoteTo <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s15/cf3b1e7> .

